<article class="env-lemma" id="09ND">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09ND">Lemma <span data-tag="09ND">33.38.6</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a Noetherian integral separated scheme of dimension $1$. Then $X$ has an ample invertible sheaf. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose an affine open covering $X = U_1 \cup \ldots \cup U_ n$. Since $X$ is Noetherian, each of the sets $X \setminus U_ i$ is finite. Thus by Lemma <a href="/tag/09NB" data-tag="09NB">33.38.4</a> we can find a pair $(\mathcal{L}_ i, s_ i)$ consisting of a globally generated invertible sheaf $\mathcal{L}_ i$ and a global section $s_ i$ such that $U_ i = X_{s_ i}$. We conclude that $X$ has an ample invertible sheaf by Lemma <a href="/tag/09NC" data-tag="09NC">33.38.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>